<div class="about-page">

  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-label">About</div>
    <h1>Software that answers to you,<br>not to a server.</h1>
    <p class="about-sub">Penumbra Forge LLC is an independent software company founded in 2026. We build privacy-first AI and security tooling — software that runs on your hardware, with your data staying yours.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>What we build</h2>
    <p>Everything we ship follows one rule: computation belongs on hardware the user controls. That spans three fronts:</p>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Local AI</h3>
        <p><a href="/umbra/">Umbra</a>, our local-first AI studio, runs and audits large language models entirely on-device — built for NVIDIA DGX Spark. On this site, our AI tools run quantized LLM inference in your browser over WebGPU, or against your own Ollama / LM Studio runtime.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Security software</h3>
        <p><a href="/gate/">Gate</a> stops secrets before they reach your repository. <a href="/vexes/">Vexes</a> catches supply-chain attacks across nine package ecosystems with behavioral analysis. <a href="/librarian/">mcp-librarian</a> gives AI coding agents a self-growing, cryptographically signed skills library.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Open instruments</h3>
        <p><a href="/tools/">77 browser-based tools</a> for security engineering, threat intel, encoding, and development — client-side by default, zero tracking, and <a href="/tools/agents/">usable by AI agents</a> through our MCP server.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Founder</h2>
    <div class="about-founder">
      <div class="about-founder-body">
        <h3>Shadoe Myers</h3>
        <p class="about-founder-role">Founder</p>
        <p>Shadoe is a senior security engineer who builds the automation and tooling behind a corporate cybersecurity incident-response team — the sole developer for its security-automation platform, custom integrations, and internal tools — with over a decade across security engineering, SOC operations, and software development. Years of watching security and AI tooling drift toward surveillance — telemetry in developer tools, prompts leaving machines, dependencies nobody audits — became the reason for Penumbra Forge: every product is open to inspection, runs locally, and treats your data as none of our business.</p>
        <div class="about-founder-links">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shadoe-myers" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a href="mailto:shadoe@penumbraforge.com">shadoe@penumbraforge.com</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul class="about-principles">
      <li><strong>Client-side by default.</strong> A tool only touches the network when its function demands it — and it says so on the label.</li>
      <li><strong>Dependencies are attack surface.</strong> Zero-dependency codebases built on platform primitives instead of framework stacks that expire.</li>
      <li><strong>Open and auditable.</strong> Small enough to audit in an afternoon. No telemetry, no accounts, no dark patterns.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section about-contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:shadoe@penumbraforge.com">shadoe@penumbraforge.com</a> — general, privacy, and security reports alike (see <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>).</p>
  </section>

</div>

